You can determine whether a sound is rising or a sound is falling. In a very, very short period of time, we can help people understand those differences of all the different key healthcare data points to understand what a patient needs or whether that patient is okay and they can turn their attention elsewhere. When I was in music school, my piano teacher told me, the more you actively listen to jazz and you practice, you're adding colors to your palate. The more I study, the more I practice, the more I listen, I have more colors on my palette. I can create a beautiful painting. And so the reason why
